content='<section class="pi-objective cd-intro"><p class="pi-label">Unit 4 · Session 9 · Complementary Grammar</p><h2>Your grammar goal</h2><p>Describe repeated celebration customs, place frequency adverbs, and describe objects, people and food with quantity expressions.</p><div class="pi-route"><span>8 customs and frequency gaps</span><span>8 description and quantity gaps</span><span>2 independent grammar exercises</span></div><p class="pi-small">These exercises were written for the course pacing guide and the Unit 4 explanation. They are complementary course material, not original grammar exercises from the ESL Pals PDF. The unchanged PDF supports the celebration theme.</p><p class="pi-small">Write only the missing words, using the clues in brackets. Complete an exercise before checking. Explanations and model audio appear after two different complete attempts, or after a perfect first attempt. Equivalent contractions, capitalisation and punctuation do not add an attempt. Each exercise keeps its own draft, reset and undo in this browser tab, including after a reload. This is practice only; no official grade or teacher submission is created.</p><p><a href="unit-4-celebrations-festivals.html#customs-frequency">Review the Unit 4 explanation</a></p><p id="cd-storage-status" class="pi-small" role="status" hidden></p></section><div class="pi-audio-controls" aria-label="Grammar practice audio controls"><span>Audio speed</span><button type="button" data-cd-speed="0.75" aria-pressed="false">0.75×</button><button type="button" data-cd-speed="1" aria-pressed="true">1.0×</button><button type="button" data-cd-speed="1.25" aria-pressed="false">1.25×</button><button type="button" data-cd-stop>Stop audio</button><span id="cd-audio-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Listen to an instruction, worked example or underlined expression.</span></div>'
